    "id": "p17-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "James A. Garfield, the twentieth president of the United States, gave the following elegant proof of the Pythagorean Theorem by considering the trapezium below.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q11-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"regionBlue\",\"hex\":\"D4E8FF\",\"reason\":\"distinguishes the central triangle in the three-triangle area decomposition\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 17 p17-q11-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{regionBlue}{HTML}{D4E8FF}\n\\coordinate (L) at (0,0); \\coordinate (T) at (0,3); \\coordinate (P) at (2,0); \\coordinate (R) at (5,0); \\coordinate (U) at (5,2);\n\\fill[regionBlue] (T)--(P)--(U)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (L)--(T)--(U)--(R)--cycle;\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (T)--(P)--(U);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ($(P)!0.24cm!(T)$)--($($(P)!0.24cm!(T)$)+($(P)!0.24cm!(U)$)-(P)$)--($(P)!0.24cm!(U)$);\n\\path (L)--(T) node[midway,left] {$b$};\n\\path (R)--(U) node[midway,right] {$a$};\n\\path (L)--(P) node[midway,below] {$a$};\n\\path (P)--(R) node[midway,below] {$b$};\n\\path (T)--(P) node[midway,above right] {$c$};\n\\path (P)--(U) node[midway,above left] {$c$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 17,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 11, upper right",
          "description": "Vertical parallel sides, split horizontal base, two equal c-labelled internal segments and their coordinate-derived right-angle marker. Light blue identifies the central triangle; the outer triangles remain unfilled.",
          "mathematics": "Parallel sides have lengths b and a, separated by a+b. The outer triangles have perpendicular legs a and b. The central triangle has perpendicular sides c and c. Drawing coordinates express these relationships without adding numerical givens.",
          "answerVisibility": "All printed givens remain visible; no area results are shown."
